# M7 Independent Layer 5 Molecular Verification Script for UCSF ChimeraX
# Usage: chimerax inspect_active_sites.cxc
#
# Epistemic & Structural Provenance Notes:
# 1. #1 (dsrB_2V4J_catalytic_cluster.pdb) is a COMPOSITE ACTIVE-SITE EXCERPT of selected
#    chain fragments from three separate source crystal structures:
#      - Chain A: DsrB (PDB 2V4J, UniProt P45575, Cys261/264/268 + [Fe4S4]/siroheme)
#      - Chain B: OahA (PDB 3M0J, UniProt A2QSW8, Arg21/Ser26 + Mg2+/oxalate)
#      - Chain C: OxDC (PDB 1J58, UniProt O34714, His95/His97/Glu101 + Mn2+/oxalate)
#    It is NOT one single crystallographic assembly of all three proteins.
# 2. For independent verification of the complete original crystallographic assemblies
#    directly from the PDB archive in ChimeraX:
#      open 2v4j 3m0j 1j58
# 3. #2 (csgA_curli_repeat_model.pdb) is badged as [THEORETICAL_MODEL_FRAGMENT]: an
#    18-residue (Ser43..Gln60) theoretical repeat fragment of E. coli CsgA (UniProt P28307),
#    contrasted with full-length experimental cryo-EM curli assemblies PDB 8ENQ / 8ENR:
#      open 8enq 8enr

open dsrB_2V4J_catalytic_cluster.pdb
open csgA_curli_repeat_model.pdb

# Optional online full-assembly retrieval (uncomment when connected to RCSB PDB):
# open 2v4j 3m0j 1j58
# open 8enq 8enr

hide atoms
cartoon
color #1/A cornflower blue
color #1/B light sea green
color #1/C medium purple
color #2 gold

# Display catalytic residues and metal/ligand cofactors as sticks
select #1/A:261,264,268 #1/A:501,502 #1/B:21,26,301,302 #1/C:95,97,101,401,402 #2/A:49,52,54,60
style sel stick
show sel atoms
~select

# Compute non-covalent contacts around DsrB, OahA, and OxdC metal cofactors
contacts #1/A:501,502 #1/B:301,302 #1/C:401,402 reveal true
surface #1/B enclose #1/B:18-28 transparency 65
view #1/A:261-268
